            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of post-herpetic neuralgia and acute herpetic pain with amitriptyline and perphenazine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>274-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A fixed-ratio combination of amitriptyline and perphenazine was successful in treating 8 of 9 patients suffering from post-herpetic neuralgia. Side-effects were minimal. Summaries of 4 case histories are presented. In addition, 3 patients suffering from severe acute herpetic pain were successfully treated with the same drug combination.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
